<title>GERMANY: Allianz names Vereinte executives.</title>
<headline>Allianz names Vereinte executives.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-11-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allianz Versicherung AG, Europe's largest insurer, said its chief executive Reiner Hagemann would become supervisory board chairman of Vereinte Versicherungsgruppe.</p>
<p>Cartel authorities recently gave the go-ahead for Allianz's takeover of Vereinte, Germany's second largest health insurance company, from its previous owner, Swiss Re.</p>
<p>Gerhard Rupprecht was named supervisory board chairman of Vereinte Kranken- and Vereinte Lebensversicherung, while Ulrich Rumm was made management board chairman of Vereinte Holding.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
